    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOLB-lzc8AAAABC3mgzw",
      "title": "docs(superchain-upgrades): disallow simultaneous upgrade activations",
      "author": "OptimismBot",
      "number": 942,
      "body": "Adds a general activation rule: two network upgrades MUST NOT activate at the same L2 block timestamp, unless that timestamp is at or before genesis (where upgrades activate in the genesis block itself and conventionally share timestamp `0`).\n\nThe restriction was already real but undocumented — nothing in the specs constrained activation-time ordering, and [`checkFork`](https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/optimism/blob/develop/op-node/rollup/types.go#L465-L480) in op-node explicitly permits equality. [ethereum-optimism/optimism#22828](https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/optimism/issues/22828) is what surfaced it: Karst and Lagoon activating at the same non-genesis timestamp both add upgrade gas, but the reconstruction helpers only subtract Karst's allocation, so the inflated gas limit persists.\n\nPer the thread discussion, the rule is stated once under \"Activation rules\" rather than repeated in each fork's own specification. Rationale captured in the text: each upgrade's activation-block behavior is only defined against a chain where every prior upgrade is active and every later one is not, so supporting overlapping activations would mean specifying and testing every combination of upgrades that could activate together.\n\nThe wording is scoped to OP-Stack network upgrades — it deliberately does not constrain an OP-Stack upgrade timestamp against an L1 fork timestamp on the same chain (e.g. Upgrade 15 sets `pragueTime == isthmusTime`).\n\nThe second commit adds a non-retroactivity note, because six chains in the superchain registry already violate the rule: Celo mainnet activated Holocene and Isthmus at `1752073200` (genesis `1742957258`), and sepolia/boba, sepolia/lisk, sepolia/mode, sepolia/race and sepolia/soneium-minato each share a post-genesis timestamp between two earlier upgrades. Their activation history cannot be changed, so the rule has to bind newly scheduled activations rather than all historical configs.\n\nCompanion monorepo PR — docs plus the strengthened rollup-config validation: [ethereum-optimism/optimism#22838](https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/optimism/pull/22838)\n\nPrompted by: @sebastianst",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/specs",
      "createdAt": "2026-09-09T17:08:55Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 31,
      "deletions": 0
    }
